Status: DONE
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/BowserBoy/issues/125
Milestone: Independent movable, collapsible console and lighting panels.
Dependencies: Existing tools-dock interaction and workstream125.
Purpose: Give the GBA/DS selector and lighting panel the same drag/collapse
interaction as the bottom tools dock without changing console or light state.

Tasks:
- [x] Reuse one shared drag/collapse implementation for all three docks.
- [x] Add independent drag handles, collapse toggles and accessible help.
- [x] Preserve console palettes, lighting actions and bottom-dock behavior.
- [x] Qualify pointer, touch, keyboard, cancellation and resized play views.
- [x] Update focused guide, development ledger and owned continuity.

Acceptance criteria:
Both new panels independently move with their handles and collapse without
changing their actions. Mouse/touch capture prevents accidental scene drags.
Arrow keys move, Shift increases steps, Home resets and Escape cancels a drag.
Moved panels remain reachable after expanding, resize and play-view changes.
Existing bottom-dock collapse, movement and console-reveal behavior remains.
The two newly movable panels retain their previous expanded initial state;
bottom tools remain initially collapsed. Positions reset on reload.
No commit, push, deployment, book rebuild or ROM publication is required.

Completion evidence:
2026-11-09: Syntax/build and64/64unit tests PASS. All eight focused dock
browser cases PASS together in1.1minutes, covering existing bottom tools,
both new panels with desktop/mobile touch, real collapsed state, keyboard,
cancellation/reset, resize/play views and unchanged GBA/DS lighting actions.
Desktop/mobile captures of both requested panels actually reviewed.
Technical qualification only; no physical-device or human-approval claim.

Completion log:
2026-11-09: User identified console selection and lighting in their screenshot.
Extract the existing tools-dock mechanism rather than copying drag logic twice.
Keep busy/load ownership and existing action IDs unchanged.
2026-11-09: Touch qualification exposed missed clicks after dragging despite
stable pickup bounds and unprevented touch events. SVG hit routing alone
did not solve this. Add touch-action:manipulation to action buttons; keep
touch-action:none only on drag handles. Both isolated mobile cases and the
subsequent complete eight-case regression pass without forced clicks,
off-center taps, sleeps or retries. Browser gesture-disambiguation behavior
is the supported explanation, not a claim of a measured browser-internal cause.
Correct lighting action inventory to exclude new handle/collapse buttons.
Source remains local/uncommitted; no deployment or book production.
